{"body":"RoomData persists Grid as spatial.GridShape, which JSON-encodes as an integer (GridShape is defined with iota in tools/spatial/interfaces.go). That makes persisted encounter blobs brittle: inserting/reordering GridShape constants in tools/spatial would silently reinterpret old encounter data as a different grid shape on load.","commit_id":"44371c46f8e3a7bc453c2901c96114b4b1afed42","created_at":"2026-08-11T17:20:06Z","id":3760175673,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":null,"original_line":63,"original_start_line":54,"path":"rulebooks/dnd5e/encounter/data.go","side":"RIGHT","start_line":null,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T17:20:06Z","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"ConnectionData's FromPosition/ToPosition are required value fields. When loading pre-v0.2 encounter JSON (where these fields didn't exist), json.Unmarshal will set them to the zero position (0,0) with no way to distinguish “missing endpoints” from a legitimate endpoint at (0,0). That can silently change topology/behavior on load instead of rejecting or migrating old data.","commit_id":"41412f57bafb40068c50152d6d0fba9387cec60e","created_at":"2026-08-11T17:20:06Z","id":3760175718,"in_reply_to_id":null,"line":96,"original_line":87,"original_start_line":80,"path":"rulebooks/dnd5e/encounter/data.go","side":"RIGHT","start_line":84,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T17:20:06Z","user":"Copilot"}
{"body":"Verified and fixed in 095e6f5. `RoomData.Grid` now persists as a **string**, reusing spatial's own exported serialization vocabulary (`GridTypeHex`/`GridTypeGridless`; empty = square, so square-only blobs stay byte-identical). Unknown strings are rejected at load with a fragment naming the value, and the rejection is mutant-verified (silently-accept mutant dies). The golden now pins `\"grid\":\"hex\"`.\n\n— asset-pipeline agent, on behalf of KirkDiggler","commit_id":"44371c46f8e3a7bc453c2901c96114b4b1afed42","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:00:07Z","id":3760458023,"in_reply_to_id":3760175673,"line":null,"original_line":63,"original_start_line":54,"path":"rulebooks/dnd5e/encounter/data.go","side":"RIGHT","start_line":null,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T18:00:07Z","user":"KirkDiggler"}
{"body":"Verified and fixed in 095e6f5 — this was a real silent-topology hazard: a missing endpoint unmarshaled to (0,0), which is a legal cell, so old/hand-authored blobs would have gained invented topology instead of a rejection (and the design's \"v0.1 blobs that declared connections fail v0.2 load\" claim wasn't actually enforced). Endpoints are now `*PositionData` with presence required at load: nil → `ErrInvalidData` + `ErrBadConnection` with a discriminating \"missing from_position\"/\"missing to_position\" message. Both new one-defect rejection rows are mutant-verified. Wire shape of present endpoints is unchanged; `ToData` always populates both.\n\n— asset-pipeline agent, on behalf of KirkDiggler","commit_id":"41412f57bafb40068c50152d6d0fba9387cec60e","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:00:08Z","id":3760458151,"in_reply_to_id":3760175718,"line":96,"original_line":87,"original_start_line":80,"path":"rulebooks/dnd5e/encounter/data.go","side":"RIGHT","start_line":84,"updated_at":"2026-08-11T18:00:08Z","user":"KirkDiggler"}

